  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN281.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉ vēṟupaṭṭa talaimakaḷatu vēṟupāṭu kaṇṭāṟṟāḷāya ṭōḻikkut talaimakaḷ colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said to the confidante who was unable to bear it when seeing the changes in HER who had undergone changes during the separation from HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN281.1">
        <l>ceyvatu teri<supplied>nti</supplied>ciṟ ṟōḻi yalkalu</l>
        <l>makalu makaḷā<supplied>ṇ</supplied>mai yac<supplied>ca</supplied>ṟa<supplied>k</supplied> kūṟiya</l>
        <l>coṟpaḻu tāku meṉṟu mañcā</l>
        <l>tol<supplied>ki</supplied>ppaṉ maṭamayi loḻitta pīli</l>
        <l>vāṉpōḻ valviṟ cuṟṟi nōṉcilai</l>
        <l>yavvār viḷimpiṟ kamainta novviyaṟ</l>
        <l>kaṉaikura licaikkum viraicelaṟ kaṭuṅka<supplied>ṇai</supplied></l>
        <l>mura<supplied>ṇ</supplied>miku vaṭukar muṉṉuṟa moḻiyar</l>
        <l>teṉṟicai mātira muṉṉiya viraviṟku</l>
        <l>viṇṇuṟa vōṅkiya paṉiyiruṅ kuṉṟat</l>
        <l>to<supplied>ṇ</supplied>katirt tikiri yuruḷiya kuṟaitta</l>
        <l>varaiyi<supplied>ṟa</supplied>n tavarō ceṉṟaṉar</l>
        <l>paṟaiyaṟain taṉṉa valarnamak koḻittē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1a-c">Understand [his] doings, friend.</l>
        <l corresp="3a-c">Although [we said] that the words were a mistake</l>
        <l corresp="1d-2">which he fearlessly spoke about the manliness of a woman who would depart at night too,</l>
        <l rend="indent8" corresp="3d">without fear</l>
        <l corresp="12">he, he went, traversing the border</l>
        <l corresp="11">that was levelled so that bright-spoked wheels would roll</l>
        <l corresp="10">over the chilly big hill that is so high as to touch the sky,</l>
        <l corresp="9">because of getting mixed up when they approached the great direction that is the southern one,</l>
        <l corresp="8">those who [gave their] word in front the Vaṭukar full of hostility,</l>
        <l corresp="7">with fierce arrows that go swiftly when [their] intense voice sounds(?),</l>
        <l corresp="6">[arrows] of thin nature suited for [defending] that long border,</l>
        <l corresp="5">[made] of sturdy Cilai wood, having tied to the sky-crossing(?) strong bow</l>
        <l corresp="4">tail feathers cast off by many youthful peacocks in exhaustion, </l>
        <l corresp="13">– putting an end for us to gossip [as loud] as a drum beaten.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
